ANS: B 
As the health care community explores the concept of health literacy, many organizations 
recognize that before improvements can be made, operational definitions are imperative. The 
realization that consumers need to be able to understand the medical information delivered by
 
health care providers has gained recognition at many governmental levels. The Healthy People 
2020 publication describes a national movement that addresses the priorities of prevention and 
public health in the United States. Health literacy with its impact on this initiative is being 
recognized and has become a key component of the project. Although low literacy and low health 
literacy are related terms, they are not interchangeable. Low health literacy is content-specific, 
meaning that the individual may not have difficulty reading and writing outside the health care 
arena. Interest in effective patient education is not a phenomenon unique to the United States. The 
Institute of Medicine Roundtable on Health Literacy held a workshop in 2012 focused on 
international health literacy. 
 
